 "pitfalls": [
  "Going to imperial and back can move a value by a unit: the steppers show whole numbers and the result uses what they show, so 171 cm becomes 67 in and then 170 cm",
  "The bands are the WHO adult cut-offs; the number is no diagnosis, and it does not apply to children",
  "step(x, edge) is 1 only above the edge, so at exactly 25.0 it says 0: the bands test the rounded BMI against 24.95 and so on, halfway between two values that can show",
  "The unit actions spell out their expressions (abs(@unit - @was), the limits): resources expressions like @hMin hold last frame's value during the tap"
 ],
